    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0788" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812,00/14674.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister to
                            Mexico to the British Ambassador at
                            Washington.</hi><anchor n="19" xml:id="d852-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs states that he is prepared to consider
                    neutralization of Mexican railways. * * * None of us here have the vaguest idea
                    of the state of affairs in the northern part of the Republic. I cannot but
                    consider present improvement in situation as trifling and temporary, the real
                    gravity of conditions has in no way diminished.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hohler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
